{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Necromancer: Life For Power shield is not rescaled by the widened battleground catch-up",
  "contract": "A level 12 Undead Necromancer (nec) and a level 29 Orc Warrior (mate) of the Horde enter a Warsong Gulch of the 10-29 bracket against two level 29 Human Warriors (a1, a2). The widened bracket lifts nec's health (+333 bare + 207 gear health = +540) and multiplies its damage, healing and absorbs by the ratio of lifted to own bare health, where a player's bare health is basehealth + 20 + 10 per Stamina above 20. From player_class_stats (CoA.ClassLevelSixtyStats.Enable defaults to 0, so ascension_class_stats is not joined; the Undead race Stamina modifier is 0): Necromancer level 12 BaseHP 170 and Stamina 30 give 170 + 20 + 100 = 290; level 29 BaseHP 393 and Stamina 41 give 393 + 20 + 210 = 623. The ratio is 623 / 290 = 2.14828 and the maximum health gain is 223 base health + 11 Stamina x 10 + 207 gear health = 540. Life For Power (705746) converts 20% of each heal taken into the shield 707194, recast with the stored amount plus the new piece and capped at maximum health before the cast. The converted piece already carries the ratio through the heal it comes from, so the shield spell itself is never scaled again: scaled_output nec to nec with 1000 healing and spell 707194 gives 1000, while an ordinary self heal (Flash Heal 2061) gives round(1000 x 2.14828) = 2148. Greater Heal 25213 (coa-dbc-viewer record: EffectBasePoints 1247, EffectDieSides 218, BaseLevel 68, ManaCostPercentage 32) heals at least 1248 before the ratio for a caster below its base level and costs 32% of the level 12 base mana 218 = 70, so nec's mana is set to 200 before each cast. Warsong Gulch autocasts PvP - Battleground - Dampening 74411 (spell_area 3277), whose effects lower healing taken (aura 136) and absorb amounts (aura 317) by 20% (EffectBasePoints -21). One heal therefore heals at least 1248 x 0.8 x 2.148 = 2145 and converts at least 428, more than half of the lifted maximum health (830), so from the second heal on each recast carries stored + room = maximum health and Dampening leaves int(0.8 x maximum health): after twelve heals the shield holds between 0.799 and 0.8 of maximum health. With the shield scaled again on each recast, the first heal alone produced about 428 x 0.8 x 2.148 = 735, and subsequent hits above maximum health would breach the cap; the shield must never exceed it after any heal. No assertion depends on a critical heal or another random roll: a critical heal only converts more, and the cap bounds it.",
